","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#websocket-package","content":"**`InternalWebSocket`** — internal connection implementation.","locale":"en"},"2003":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-40","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#websocket-package","content":"Loads its own platform-specific `.node` from the same `native/` search paths.","locale":"en"},"2004":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-41","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#sdk-package","content":"`@snowluma/sdk` is a typed OneBot client for downstream consumers — standalone-publishable to npm and independent of the SnowLuma runtime. It's built inside the monorepo (see `pnpm build:sdk` / `build:all` below); for consumer-side usage see the SDK docs.","locale":"en"},"2005":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-42","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#build-order","content":"Full distribution:","locale":"en"},"2006":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-43","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#build-order","content":"Runs, in order:","locale":"en"},"2007":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-44","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#build-order","content":"`@snowluma/core` full build","locale":"en"},"2008":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-45","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#build-order","content":"`@snowluma/sdk`","locale":"en"},"2009":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-46","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#build-order","content":"`webui`","locale":"en"},"2010":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-47","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#build-order","content":"Output goes to the repo root `dist/`.","locale":"en"},"2011":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-48","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#docs-site","content":"The docs site lives in a separate repo: `SnowLuma/SnowLumaDocs`. Local development usually checks it out at `dev/SnowLumaDocs/` alongside SnowLuma.","locale":"en"},"2012":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-49","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#docs-site","content":"Stack: Rspress + React + TypeScript + MDX + KaTeX.","locale":"en"},"2013":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-50","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#docs-site","content":"The OneBot API reference is generated by the docs repo's `pnpm api:generate` (also wired to `prebuild`) from `docs/public/api/catalog.json` — one page per action, plus a category overview and a searchable landing page. `catalog.json` is the action catalog produced by the main repo's `collectActionDocs()` (same shape as `@snowluma/mcp`'s `CatalogAction`); the main repo's `sync-docs-catalog` workflow commits it here automatically via the SnowLuma bot on release — no manual upkeep.","locale":"en"},"2014":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-51","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#contribution-notes","content":"**Don't bypass `BridgeManager`** — every OneBot action should reach NTQQ through `BridgeInterface`. Keeps the OneBot layer decoupled and testable.","locale":"en"},"2015":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-52","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#contribution-notes","content":"**Keep configs auto-generatable** — new fields must stay backwards-compatible; normalize them on load and write the result back.","locale":"en"},"2016":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-53","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#contribution-notes","content":"**Native modules are per-platform** — when adding a platform, sync the `.node` and the injectable library.","locale":"en"},"2017":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-54","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#contribution-notes","content":"**Tests first** — core OneBot behavior should be validated with `vitest`; see `packages/core/tests/`.","locale":"en"},"2018":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/developer-55","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/developer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/developer#contribution-notes","content":"**API docs automation** — just add the action with `defineAction` (optionally `returnsSchema` to describe `data`); `catalog.json` is kept in sync by the `sync-docs-catalog` workflow, so the API reference never drifts. Run `pnpm api:generate` locally to preview.","locale":"en"},"2019":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","type":"page","content":"Troubleshooting","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/faq","locale":"en"},"2020":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/faq","content":"QR login, passwords, ports, injection, and image pulls","locale":"en"},"2021":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#novnc-never-connects--spins-forever","content":"noVNC never connects / spins forever","locale":"en"},"2022":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#cannot-find-the-webui-password","content":"Cannot find the WebUI password","locale":"en"},"2023":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#a-bot-cannot-reach-3000--3001","content":"A bot cannot reach 3000 / 3001","locale":"en"},"2024":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-4","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#injection-fails--qq-runs-but-never-comes-online","content":"Injection fails / QQ runs but never comes online","locale":"en"},"2025":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-5","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#image-pull-hangs-in-china","content":"Image pull hangs in China","locale":"en"},"2026":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-6","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#upgrade-asks-you-to-scan-again","content":"Upgrade asks you to scan again","locale":"en"},"2027":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-7","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#novnc-never-connects--spins-forever","content":"Confirm port `6081` is published. Official templates **do not** publish `5900`.","locale":"en"},"2028":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-8","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#novnc-never-connects--spins-forever","content":"There is **no** shared default remote-desktop password. The first start generates a random one and prints it once; later restarts will not print it again — use the value you saved.","locale":"en"},"2029":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-9","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#novnc-never-connects--spins-forever","content":"High CPU and no handshake: pass `--ulimit nofile=65536:1048576` (already in official compose).","locale":"en"},"2030":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-10","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#cannot-find-the-webui-password","content":"The bootstrap password is printed only on the **first start of a fresh data volume**. Reusing a volume will not print a new one.","locale":"en"},"2031":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-11","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#a-bot-cannot-reach-3000--3001","content":"In Docker, OneBot should listen on `0.0.0.0`. Upgrading the image rewrites a leftover loopback default; a host you set yourself is left alone.","locale":"en"},"2032":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-12","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#a-bot-cannot-reach-3000--3001","content":"On the compose network use the service name `snowluma`, not `127.0.0.1`.","locale":"en"},"2033":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-13","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#a-bot-cannot-reach-3000--3001","content":"Send the access token.","locale":"en"},"2034":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-14","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#injection-fails--qq-runs-but-never-comes-online","content":"You still need `SYS_PTRACE` and `seccomp=unconfined`.","locale":"en"},"2035":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-15","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#injection-fails--qq-runs-but-never-comes-online","content":"Do not start a second QQ as root inside the container.","locale":"en"},"2036":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-16","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#injection-fails--qq-runs-but-never-comes-online","content":"`ptrace_scope=3` refuses ptrace outright.","locale":"en"},"2037":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-17","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#injection-fails--qq-runs-but-never-comes-online","content":"Do not delete the `qq-gateway-data`, `qq-client-config`, or `qq-client-data` volumes.","locale":"en"},"2038":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-18","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#image-pull-hangs-in-china","content":"That hop is Docker Hub. The installer retries with prefixes. Manually:","locale":"en"},"2039":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-19","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#image-pull-hangs-in-china","content":"On 1Panel / Baota, set a registry mirror in the panel. The installer will not rewrite `daemon.json`.","locale":"en"},"2040":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/faq-20","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/faq#upgrade-asks-you-to-scan-again","content":"Recreating the container can look like a new device. Keep the volumes. If you still must log in again, scan via noVNC.","locale":"en"},"2041":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","type":"page","content":"Introduction","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","locale":"en"},"2042":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","content":"What SnowLuma is, what you can do with it, and its three usage shapes and release layout","locale":"en"},"2043":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#three-usage-shapes","content":"Three usage shapes","locale":"en"},"2044":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#release-layout","content":"Release layout","locale":"en"},"2045":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#default-services","content":"Default services","locale":"en"},"2046":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-4","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#project-status","content":"Project status","locale":"en"},"2047":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-5","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#next-steps","content":"Next steps","locale":"en"},"2048":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-6","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","content":"SnowLuma is a **remote-protocol framework** for NTQQ (the QQ desktop client). It bridges QQ into the OneBot v11 ecosystem: a native addon injects a hook into the running QQ process via ptrace-class injection (Linux process `qq`, Windows `QQ.exe`), decodes its internal packets, and exposes them as OneBot v11 over HTTP / WebSocket / reverse-WS / HTTP-POST.","locale":"en"},"2049":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-7","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","content":"Around that core, SnowLuma also ships:","locale":"en"},"2050":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-8","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","content":"**OneBot v11 adapters** — HTTP API server, WebSocket server, reverse WebSocket, and HTTP event reporting, in any combination.","locale":"en"},"2051":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-9","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","content":"**NTQQ bridge** — talks to the real QQ client directly; no protocol account, no separate login.","locale":"en"},"2052":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-10","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","content":"**Multi-account** — one OneBot instance per UIN, auto-detected and auto-attached, no manual config.","locale":"en"},"2053":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-11","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","content":"**Built-in WebUI** — manage accounts, config, and status from the browser.","locale":"en"},"2054":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-12","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","content":"**TypeScript SDK** — `@snowluma/sdk`, for writing fully typed OneBot clients.","locale":"en"},"2055":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-13","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","content":"**MCP server** — `@snowluma/mcp`, so MCP-capable AI clients can query and invoke OneBot actions.","locale":"en"},"2056":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-14","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#three-usage-shapes","content":"Your goal","locale":"en"},"2057":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-15","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#three-usage-shapes","content":"Shape","locale":"en"},"2058":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-16","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#three-usage-shapes","content":"Start here","locale":"en"},"2059":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-17","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#three-usage-shapes","content":"Run a bot long-term on a server","locale":"en"},"2060":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-18","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#three-usage-shapes","content":"**Docker** (recommended)","locale":"en"},"2061":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-19","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#three-usage-shapes","content":"Docker deployment","locale":"en"},"2062":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-20","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#three-usage-shapes","content":"Let an AI client drive QQ","locale":"en"},"2063":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-21","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#three-usage-shapes","content":"**MCP**","locale":"en"},"2064":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-22","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#three-usage-shapes","content":"MCP integration","locale":"en"},"2065":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-23","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#three-usage-shapes","content":"Try it quickly on a local machine","locale":"en"},"2066":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-24","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#three-usage-shapes","content":"**Prebuilt tarball**","locale":"en"},"2067":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-25","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#three-usage-shapes","content":"Choose a deployment","locale":"en"},"2068":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-26","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#three-usage-shapes","content":"To write client code, see the TypeScript SDK.","locale":"en"},"2069":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-27","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#release-layout","content":"Each platform ships two tarball flavors on GitHub Releases:","locale":"en"},"2070":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-28","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#release-layout","content":"Filename","locale":"en"},"2071":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-29","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#release-layout","content":"Bundles Node.js?","locale":"en"},"2072":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-30","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#release-layout","content":"When to use","locale":"en"},"2073":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-31","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#release-layout","content":"`SnowLuma-<TAG>-<platform>-<arch>.tar.gz` (**full**)","locale":"en"},"2074":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-32","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#release-layout","content":"Yes, bundles a Node runtime","locale":"en"},"2075":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-33","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#release-layout","content":"No Node installed; runs out of the box","locale":"en"},"2076":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-34","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#release-layout","content":"`SnowLuma-<TAG>-<platform>-<arch>-lite.tar.gz` (**lite**)","locale":"en"},"2077":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-35","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#release-layout","content":"No (much smaller)","locale":"en"},"2078":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-36","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#release-layout","content":"Node.js ≥ 22 already installed (Node 24 LTS recommended)","locale":"en"},"2079":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-37","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#release-layout","content":"Published platforms / arches: `linux-x64`, `linux-arm64`, `win-x64`.","locale":"en"},"2080":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-38","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/introduction#release-layout","content":"SnowLuma requires **Node.js ≥ 22**. As of 2026, **Node 24 (\"Krypton\") is Active LTS** and 22 (\"Jod\") is Maintenance LTS, so for the lite tarball install **Node 24 LTS** (22 still works). The full tarball bundles its own runtime — no install needed. Source: nodejs.org.","locale":"en"},"2081":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/introduction-39","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/introducti