url":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart#fastest-path-docker","content":"`--cap-add=SYS_PTRACE` and `--security-opt seccomp=unconfined` are **required**. `--shm-size=1g` is required by QQ. The remote-desktop password is generated on first start and printed once in the logs.","locale":"en"},"2143":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart-36","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart#fastest-path-docker","content":"**2. Scan the login QR**","locale":"en"},"2144":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart-37","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart#fastest-path-docker","content":"Open `http://<server-ip>:6081/` (noVNC). Password:","locale":"en"},"2145":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart-38","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart#fastest-path-docker","content":"QQ is already running on the remote desktop — scan with the QQ mobile app.","locale":"en"},"2146":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart-39","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart#fastest-path-docker","content":"**3. Open the WebUI**","locale":"en"},"2147":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart-40","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart#fastest-path-docker","content":"Open `http://<server-ip>:5099/`. Full Compose and multi-account notes: Docker deployment.","locale":"en"},"2148":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart-41","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart#experimental-one-click-installer-alpha","content":"**Not the default.** This script is in Alpha and will change. If you already have Docker, use the section above. If you want to help test it:","locale":"en"},"2149":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart-42","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart#experimental-one-click-installer-alpha","content":"Interactive mode asks which path; `--yes` without `--mode` defaults to docker. Details: One-click install (experimental).","locale":"en"},"2150":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart-43","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart#login-and-first-access","content":"Whichever path you take, first-time setup always involves these:","locale":"en"},"2151":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart-44","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart#login-and-first-access","content":"**QR login**: SnowLuma is **QR-scan login only** — there's no CLI login. On headless setups you must see the QQ window via VNC / noVNC to scan.","locale":"en"},"2152":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart-45","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart#login-and-first-access","content":"**Find the WebUI temp password**: on the **first** start with a fresh data dir, a one-time admin password is printed to the logs. Docker:","locale":"en"},"2153":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart-46","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart#login-and-first-access","content":"The temp password is printed only on the first start with a fresh data dir. Restarting or reusing an existing data dir will not regenerate it.","locale":"en"},"2154":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart-47","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart#login-and-first-access","content":"**Open ports**: to reach it from outside, allow the WebUI (`5099`) and whichever OneBot ports you use (`3000` / `3001`).","locale":"en"},"2155":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart-48","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart#login-and-first-access","content":"Do **not** expose noVNC / WebUI / OneBot ports raw on the public internet. There is no shared default remote-desktop password — read it from the container logs.","locale":"en"},"2156":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart-49","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart#password-free-login-url-token","content":"Tired of typing the password every visit? The WebUI can sign in directly from a **password** carried in the URL:","locale":"en"},"2157":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart-50","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart#password-free-login-url-token","content":"The query key is `token`, and its **value is your normal WebUI login password**. SnowLuma runs it through the login endpoint; a correct password lands you straight on the home page.","locale":"en"},"2158":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart-51","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart#password-free-login-url-token","content":"**Consumed once**: the password is **stripped from the address bar immediately** after load (`history.replaceState`) so it can't leak via browser history / access logs / the Referer header.","locale":"en"},"2159":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart-52","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart#password-free-login-url-token","content":"The server still verifies it as usual — a wrong password just drops back to the login page, there's no bypass.","locale":"en"},"2160":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart-53","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart#password-free-login-url-token","content":"Putting a password in a URL is **relatively risky** (it enters browser history and may be recorded by intermediate proxies). Only use it on a trusted local / LAN machine; don't share password links, don't paste them into chats / issues, and don't use them on a shared device.","locale":"en"},"2161":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart-54","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart#next","content":"Choose a deployment — detailed comparison of every path.","locale":"en"},"2162":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart-55","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart#next","content":"Configuration reference — ports, access tokens, adapters.","locale":"en"},"2163":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart-56","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/quickstart#next","content":"Updating — upgrade without losing your login.","locale":"en"},"2164":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions","type":"page","content":"Action Discovery and Results","breadcrumbs":["Docs","MCP"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/mcp/actions","locale":"en"},"2165":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions-0","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/actions","content":"Find actions, inspect result schemas, check configuration, and trace calls","locale":"en"},"2166":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions-1","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/mcp/actions#search-and-pagination","content":"Search and pagination","locale":"en"},"2167":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions-2","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/mcp/actions#parameters-return-schemas-and-examples","content":"Parameters, return schemas, and examples","locale":"en"},"2168":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions-3","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/mcp/actions#structured-results","content":"Structured results","locale":"en"},"2169":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions-4","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/mcp/actions#runtime-overview","content":"Runtime overview","locale":"en"},"2170":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions-5","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/mcp/actions#caching-and-tracing","content":"Caching and tracing","locale":"en"},"2171":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions-6","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/actions#search-and-pagination","content":"`search_actions` keeps case-insensitive substring matching and catalog order by default. Example tool arguments:","locale":"en"},"2172":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions-7","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/actions#search-and-pagination","content":"Keyword mode combines space-separated terms with AND, recognizes a small set of common Chinese/English synonyms, and ranks exact names or aliases first. It is not unrestricted semantic search.","locale":"en"},"2173":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions-8","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/actions#search-and-pagination","content":"Both `list_actions` and `search_actions` accept `category`, `read_only`, `stream`, `limit` (1–200), and `offset` (non-negative). Without pagination they retain `{ count, actions }`; with pagination they add matching `total` and `next_offset`, which is `null` on the last page. These tools read the bundled catalog only.","locale":"en"},"2174":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions-9","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/actions#parameters-return-schemas-and-examples","content":"`get_action({ \"name\": \"get_msg\" })` exposes `inputSchema`, `returnsSchema`, constraints, and `examples`. Replace sample account, group, message, and file identifiers with values from the current session.","locale":"en"},"2175":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions-10","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/actions#parameters-return-schemas-and-examples","content":"`returnsSchema` describes successful &#x2A;*OneBot `data`**, not the full envelope or MCP wrapper. Stream schemas describe individual frames; MCP downloads instead return saved-file metadata. Unsupported actions and compatibility placeholders are explicitly identified.","locale":"en"},"2176":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions-11","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/actions#parameters-return-schemas-and-examples","content":"Ordinary message IDs are non-zero signed 32-bit integers; negative values are valid. Example `query_action` arguments:","locale":"en"},"2177":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions-12","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/actions#parameters-return-schemas-and-examples","content":"Do not take absolute values or replace negative IDs with zero. Preserve decimal-string identifiers and sizes, as well as `null`, as documented.","locale":"en"},"2178":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions-13","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/actions#structured-results","content":"Completed calls preserve their existing `content` text and also provide `structuredContent`:","locale":"en"},"2179":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions-14","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/actions#structured-results","content":"`result` holds the original payload. Catalog tools may return arrays or indexes rather than OneBot envelopes. MCP tool errors set it to `null`. `diagnostics.outcome` is `success`, `failed`, or `unknown`; failures may include `kind`, `message`, and `next_step`.","locale":"en"},"2180":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions-15","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/actions#structured-results","content":"Ordinary OneBot business failures retain their envelope without setting `isError`, so **checking `isError` alone is insufficient**. Asynchronous acknowledgements and unconfirmed outcomes are `unknown`. Transport, argument, and stream protocol errors set `isError: true`.","locale":"en"},"2181":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions-16","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/actions#structured-results","content":"Modern `input_required` and `task` results are continuations. Check `resultType` first, then complete input collection or fetch the task's terminal result.","locale":"en"},"2182":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions-17","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/actions#runtime-overview","content":"`get_runtime_info({})` stays offline by default. It reports the effective mode, execution/write availability, catalog version, and—in execution mode—transfer limits and local directories. It does not expose the endpoint or token. `server_support: \"unknown\"` and `connection_checked: false` are not evidence of a connection or login.","locale":"en"},"2183":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions-18","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/actions#runtime-overview","content":"The following explicit option runs three read-only queries: `get_login_info`, `get_status`, and `get_version_info`:","locale":"en"},"2184":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions-19","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/actions#runtime-overview","content":"This is available only in read/write mode. Original responses and diagnostics remain under `checks`, including partial failures. A successful HTTP exchange alone does not establish that the account is online.","locale":"en"},"2185":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions-20","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/actions#caching-and-tracing","content":"Modern clients receive five-minute private cache hints for tool discovery and static resource lists, and five-minute public hints for the bundled catalog and preview UI. Enabling events disables resource-list caching. Event resources are not cached; tool execution results receive no cache hints. Legacy replies omit modern-only cache fields.","locale":"en"},"2186":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions-21","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/actions#caching-and-tracing","content":"Each tool call returns a correlation identifier in `_meta.traceparent`. Callers may provide a valid `traceparent` and optional `tracestate` in request `_meta` to retain upstream correlation. HTTP headers carry the trace; action parameters do not.","locale":"en"},"2187":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions-22","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/actions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/actions#caching-and-tracing","content":"With TRACE logging enabled in SnowLuma, match `traceparent` to `http_trace`, then follow its local request number. MCP diagnostics record the tool, outcome, duration, and failure category, not message contents or tokens. Traces are not authorization credentials and no telemetry exporter is installed.","locale":"en"},"2188":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/events","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/events","type":"page","content":"Live Event Subscriptions","breadcrumbs":["Docs","MCP"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/mcp/events","locale":"en"},"2189":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/events-0","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/events","content":"Filter OneBot events by account and conversation, then read updates with resource cursors","locale":"en"},"2190":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/events-1","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/events","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/mcp/events#configure-the-event-connection","content":"Configure the event connection","locale":"en"},"2191":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/events-2","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/events","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/mcp/events#create-a-subscription","content":"Create a subscription","locale":"en"},"2192":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/events-3","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/events","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/mcp/events#read-events","content":"Read events","locale":"en"},"2193":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/events-4","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/events","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/mcp/events#receive-change-notifications","content":"Receive change notifications","locale":"en"},"2194":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/events-5","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/events","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/mcp/events#buffer-limits-and-gaps","content":"Buffer limits and gaps","locale":"en"},"2195":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/events-6","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/events#configure-the-event-connection","content":"In read or write mode, set `SNOWLUMA_MCP_EVENTS_URL`, for example `ws://127.0.0.1:3001/event`. This is a OneBot event endpoint, not an MCP or WebUI address. It is configured separately from HTTP and reuses `SNOWLUMA_MCP_TOKEN` in an authorization header.","locale":"en"},"2196":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/events-7","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/events#configure-the-event-connection","content":"Only `ws:` / `wss:` URLs without embedded credentials, query parameters, or fragments are accepted. Listing tools or resources stays offline; `subscribe_events` opens the connection. Docs mode never connects to the event source.","locale":"en"},"2197":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/events-8","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/events#create-a-subscription","content":"Determine the expected account using `get_login_info` or an equivalent check, then call `subscribe_events`:","locale":"en"},"2198":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/events-9","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/events#create-a-subscription","content":"Identifiers above are examples. Required `self_id` must match received events; a mismatch stops the connection and is reported. Resources on one MCP connection share one account's event source.","locale":"en"},"2199":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/events-10","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/events#create-a-subscription","content":"Optional types are `message`, `notice`, and `request`; omission selects all three. `message_sent` belongs to the message category. Group and user filters combine with AND. A group filter excludes private messages and other events without `group_id`. Each ID filter accepts at most 100 distinct positive safe integers.","locale":"en"},"2200":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/events-11","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/events#read-events","content":"The successful result's `structuredContent.result.uri` is a resource address of the form `snowluma://onebot/events/<id>`. Read the actual returned URI with `resources/read`:","locale":"en"},"2201":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/events-12","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/events#read-events","content":"Resource `contents[].text` contains JSON with `status`, `events`, `next_cursor`, `oldest_cursor`, `dropped_events`, `gap`, and `notification_failed`. Retain `next_cursor` and append it as `?after=` to subsequent reads of the same resource:","locale":"en"},"2202":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/events-13","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/events#read-events","content":"Cursors belong to individual resources and cannot be reused across them. Reads do not consume events. Only events arriving after subscription creation are retained; this is not a message-history API.","locale":"en"},"2203":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/events-14","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/events#receive-change-notifications","content":"Modern clients use `subscriptions/listen`; the TypeScript client exposes `client.listen({ resourceSubscriptions: [uri] })`.","locale":"en"},"2204":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/events-15","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/events#receive-change-notifications","content":"Legacy clients first call `resources/subscribe`, then receive `notifications/resources/updated`.","locale":"en"},"2205":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/events-16","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/events#receive-change-notifications","content":"A notification says the resource changed; read it again to obtain events. &#x2A;*Notification subscriptions must use the canonical URI without `?after`.**","locale":"en"},"2206":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/events-17","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/events#receive-change-notifications","content":"Stopping a modern notification stream does not release its event buffer. Both generations can call the `unsubscribe_events` tool with `{ \"uri\": \"actual resource URI\" }`; legacy `resources/unsubscribe` also releases it. Removing the last resource closes the WebSocket. Closing MCP releases all event resources owned by that connection.","locale":"en"},"2207":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/events-18","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/events#buffer-limits-and-gaps","content":"Each resource retains at most 256 events and 1 MiB. One connection supports at most 16 resources, with a 256 KiB incoming-frame limit. Slow readers may lose older buffered entries. Check `gap`, `dropped_events`, and `oldest_cursor` rather than treating the current queue as a complete record.","locale":"en"},"2208":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/events-19","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/events#buffer-limits-and-gaps","content":"Connection failure, account mismatch, malformed input, and disconnection remain visible in status or errors. There is no silent reconnection. Release existing resources before reconnecting or switching accounts; subscribing again does not recover missing events. Failed notification delivery sets `notification_failed`.","locale":"en"},"2209":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/events-20","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/events","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/events#buffer-limits-and-gaps","content":"Subscriptions execute no OneBot business action and send no QQ messages. Any subsequent reply belongs to the caller's workflow.","locale":"en"},"2210":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","type":"page","content":"MCP Usage","breadcrumbs":["Docs","MCP"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/mcp","locale":"en"},"2211":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-0","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp","content":"Configure SnowLuma MCP for action discovery, execution, background transfers, and event subscriptions","locale":"en"},"2212":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-1","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/mcp#modes","content":"Modes","locale":"en"},"2213":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-2","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/mcp#requirements","content":"Requirements","locale":"en"},"2214":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-3","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/mcp#docs-only-mode","content":"Docs-only mode","locale":"en"},"2215":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-4","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/mcp#connect-to-snowluma","content":"Connect to SnowLuma","locale":"en"},"2216":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-5","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/mcp#enable-write-mode","content":"Enable write mode","locale":"en"},"2217":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-6","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/mcp#environment-variables","content":"Environment variables","locale":"en"},"2218":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-7","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/mcp#suggested-workflow","content":"Suggested workflow","locale":"en"},"2219":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-8","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/mcp#safety-boundaries","content":"Safety boundaries","locale":"en"},"2220":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-9","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp","content":"`@snowluma/mcp` exposes SnowLuma's OneBot action catalog and optional execution through stdio. Existing tool names, parameters, text results, and read/write gates remain compatible. Capable clients can also use input completion, background tasks, event subscriptions, and a message preview panel.","locale":"en"},"2221":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-10","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp","content":"This section follows the current development branch. New capabilities require a package containing those changes; a source update does not establish npm availability. Check your installed release. The bundled catalog is a snapshot, not proof that a connected server supports every action.","locale":"en"},"2222":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-11","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#modes","content":"Mode","locale":"en"},"2223":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-12","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#modes","content":"Activation","locale":"en"},"2224":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-13","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#modes","content":"Capabilities","locale":"en"},"2225":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-14","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#modes","content":"`docs`","locale":"en"},"2226":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-15","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#modes","content":"No endpoint, or explicitly selected","locale":"en"},"2227":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-16","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#modes","content":"Catalog, local runtime overview, and message drafts; no contact with a running SnowLuma instance.","locale":"en"},"2228":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-17","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#modes","content":"`read`","locale":"en"},"2229":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-18","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#modes","content":"Default with an endpoint","locale":"en"},"2230":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-19","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#modes","content":"Adds actions explicitly marked read-only and optional event subscriptions.","locale":"en"},"2231":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-20","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#modes","content":"`write`","locale":"en"},"2232":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-21","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#modes","content":"Explicit `SNOWLUMA_MCP_MODE=write`","locale":"en"},"2233":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-22","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#modes","content":"Adds writes and streaming; configured tasks also require a capable client.","locale":"en"},"2234":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-23","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#modes","content":"Classification comes from action definitions, not name prefixes such as `get_`. Every execution checks the mode even when a client calls an unlisted tool directly. All current stream actions, including downloads, require write mode.","locale":"en"},"2235":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-24","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#requirements","content":"A client supporting stdio MCP servers.","locale":"en"},"2236":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-25","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#requirements","content":"Node.js `^24.22.1 || >=26.12.1`, with `node` or `npx` available to that client.","locale":"en"},"2237":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-26","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#requirements","content":"Execution requires the configured **OneBot HTTP endpoint**, such as `http://127.0.0.1:3000/`, not the WebUI management port.","locale":"en"},"2238":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-27","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#requirements","content":"Events require a separately configured OneBot WebSocket event endpoint; its address is not inferred from HTTP.","locale":"en"},"2239":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-28","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#requirements","content":"The same command supports MCP `2026-07-28` discovery and legacy initialization. Existing clients keep their launch configuration. Advanced features also depend on declared client capabilities. This command does not expose a listening MCP HTTP server.","locale":"en"},"2240":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-29","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#docs-only-mode","content":"For clients using the `mcpServers` configuration format:","locale":"en"},"2241":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-30","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#docs-only-mode","content":"Tool","locale":"en"},"2242":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-31","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#docs-only-mode","content":"Purpose","locale":"en"},"2243":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-32","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#docs-only-mode","content":"`list_actions`","locale":"en"},"2244":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-33","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#docs-only-mode","content":"Filter by category, read-only status, or streaming; optionally paginate.","locale":"en"},"2245":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-34","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#docs-only-mode","content":"`search_actions`","locale":"en"},"2246":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-35","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#docs-only-mode","content":"Substring search by default; optional keywords and common Chinese/English synonyms.","locale":"en"},"2247":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-36","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#docs-only-mode","content":"`get_action`","locale":"en"},"2248":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-37","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#docs-only-mode","content":"Parameters, constraints, result schemas, and examples; aliases accepted.","locale":"en"},"2249":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-38","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#docs-only-mode","content":"`list_categories`","locale":"en"},"2250":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-39","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#docs-only-mode","content":"Categories and action counts.","locale":"en"},"2251":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-40","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#docs-only-mode","content":"`get_runtime_info`","locale":"en"},"2252":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-41","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#docs-only-mode","content":"Local overview by default; explicit connection checks require execution mode.","locale":"en"},"2253":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-42","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#docs-only-mode","content":"`preview_message`","locale":"en"},"2254":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-43","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#docs-only-mode","content":"Plain-text and quoted-reply drafts; calling the tool sends nothing.","locale":"en"},"2255":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-44","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#docs-only-mode","content":"The `snowluma://onebot/actions` resource contains the complete catalog. See Action discovery and results.","locale":"en"},"2256":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-45","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#connect-to-snowluma","content":"Check the OneBot HTTP address and access token in the WebUI network adapter settings. This enables read-only execution:","locale":"en"},"2257":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-46","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#connect-to-snowluma","content":"`127.0.0.1` refers to the machine running MCP. Use the actual server address for remote connections. Inject credentials through client configuration rather than prompts.","locale":"en"},"2258":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-47","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#connect-to-snowluma","content":"Execution mode provides `query_action({ action, params? })` and `query_action_with_input`, which can ask the user for missing required parameters. Complete arguments still work with the original tool.","locale":"en"},"2259":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-48","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#enable-write-mode","content":"Add `\"SNOWLUMA_MCP_MODE\": \"write\"` to `env` to expose `invoke_action({ action, params?, execution? })` and `invoke_action_with_input`. Writes can send messages or change group settings; control their use through your client's authorization policy.","locale":"en"},"2260":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-49","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#enable-write-mode","content":"The following `env` also enables optional services. Keep only the services you need. Directories are on the **MCP host**:","locale":"en"},"2261":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-50","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#environment-variables","content":"Variable","locale":"en"},"2262":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-51","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#environment-variables","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"2263":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-52","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#environment-variables","content":"`SNOWLUMA_MCP_ENDPOINT`","locale":"en"},"2264":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-53","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#environment-variables","content":"OneBot HTTP endpoint; absent means docs-only mode.","locale":"en"},"2265":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-54","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#environment-variables","content":"`SNOWLUMA_MCP_TOKEN`","locale":"en"},"2266":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-55","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#environment-variables","content":"Token shared by HTTP and event connections, sent in authorization headers.","locale":"en"},"2267":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-56","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#environment-variables","content":"`SNOWLUMA_MCP_MODE`","locale":"en"},"2268":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-57","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#environment-variables","content":"`docs`, `read`, or `write`.","locale":"en"},"2269":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-58","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#environment-variables","content":"`SNOWLUMA_MCP_TIMEOUT_MS`","locale":"en"},"2270":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-59","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#environment-variables","content":"Default `30000` ms. Ordinary request timeout; separate connection and per-read idle deadlines for streams.","locale":"en"},"2271":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-60","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#environment-variables","content":"`SNOWLUMA_MCP_STREAM_DIR`","locale":"en"},"2272":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-61","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#environment-variables","content":"Download output directory; defaults to `onebot-mcp-downloads` inside the system temporary directory.","locale":"en"},"2273":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-62","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#environment-variables","content":"`SNOWLUMA_MCP_UPLOAD_ROOT`","locale":"en"},"2274":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-63","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#environment-variables","content":"Existing directory allowed for automatic uploads; omitted means automatic local-file upload is disabled.","locale":"en"},"2275":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-64","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#environment-variables","content":"`SNOWLUMA_MCP_MAX_STREAM_BYTES`","locale":"en"},"2276":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-65","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#environment-variables","content":"Positive per-file byte limit, at most and defaulting to `4294967296`.","locale":"en"},"2277":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-66","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#environment-variables","content":"`SNOWLUMA_MCP_TASK_DIR`","locale":"en"},"2278":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-67","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#environment-variables","content":"Absolute private directory for task records; requires write mode and an endpoint.","locale":"en"},"2279":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-68","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#environment-variables","content":"`SNOWLUMA_MCP_EVENTS_URL`","locale":"en"},"2280":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-69","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#environment-variables","content":"Explicit `ws:` / `wss:` event address, without credentials, query parameters, or fragments.","locale":"en"},"2281":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-70","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#suggested-workflow","content":"Find actions with `search_actions`; inspect parameters, result schemas, and identifier sources with `get_action`.","locale":"en"},"2282":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-71","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#suggested-workflow","content":"Inspect configuration with `get_runtime_info`; set `check_connection: true` only when a live check is intended.","locale":"en"},"2283":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-72","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#suggested-workflow","content":"Use `query_action` for reads and `invoke_action` for writes. Their `_with_input` variants can collect missing required parameters.","locale":"en"},"2284":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-73","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#suggested-workflow","content":"Use background tasks for long transfers and event subscriptions for later messages.","locale":"en"},"2285":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-74","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#suggested-workflow","content":"Inspect business responses and diagnostics; a completed call is not proof of message delivery.","locale":"en"},"2286":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-75","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#suggested-workflow","content":"Continue with:","locale":"en"},"2287":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-76","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#suggested-workflow","content":"Action discovery, structured results, and tracing","locale":"en"},"2288":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-77","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#suggested-workflow","content":"File transfers and persistent tasks","locale":"en"},"2289":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-78","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#suggested-workflow","content":"Input completion and message previews","locale":"en"},"2290":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-79","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#suggested-workflow","content":"Live event subscriptions","locale":"en"},"2291":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp-80","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp#safety-boundaries","content":"Actions must exist in the bundled catalog and pass the mode gate. Catalog queries and the default overview stay offline; event sockets open only when the subscription tool is called. Cancellation or timeout does not undo remote effects and does not cause an automatic retry. Ordinary business failures retain the OneBot envelope: inspect `status`, `retcode`, and structured diagnostics. Parameter, transport, and stream protocol errors remain explicit failures.","locale":"en"},"2292":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction","type":"page","content":"Input Completion and Message Previews","breadcrumbs":["Docs","MCP"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction","locale":"en"},"2293":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction-0","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction","content":"Collect missing required parameters and review a message draft before sending","locale":"en"},"2294":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction-1","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction#collect-missing-parameters","content":"Collect missing parameters","locale":"en"},"2295":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction-2","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction#client-compatibility","content":"Client compatibility","locale":"en"},"2296":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction-3","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction#preview-a-message-draft","content":"Preview a message draft","locale":"en"},"2297":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction-4","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction#interactive-panel","content":"Interactive panel","locale":"en"},"2298":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction-5","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction#collect-missing-parameters","content":"`query_action_with_input` and `invoke_action_with_input` retain the original tools' arguments, catalog lookup, and mode gates. They request input only for absent top-level fields in the catalog's `required` array; they do not infer conditional requirements or optional values. Existing execution tools gain no new prompt step.","locale":"en"},"2299":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction-6","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction#collect-missing-parameters","content":"Example `invoke_action_with_input` arguments:","locale":"en"},"2300":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction-7","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction#collect-missing-parameters","content":"A form-capable client asks for the missing message. The current form has one `params_json` string field containing a JSON object such as:","locale":"en"},"2301":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction-8","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction#collect-missing-parameters","content":"Answers cannot overwrite provided parameters, the action name, or execution options. Extra fields and invalid values cause errors. Declined, cancelled, or invalid answers do not execute the action. Complete parameters execute directly; program-generated automatic-upload fields do not need user input.","locale":"en"},"2302":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction-9","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction#client-compatibility","content":"Clients must declare form elicitation support. Modern protocol calls return `resultType: \"input_required\"`; the client resumes with the protocol's request state and input response. Capable legacy clients use `elicitation/create`. Continuation results are not final OneBot responses.","locale":"en"},"2303":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction-10","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction#client-compatibility","content":"Clients without form support receive an explicit tool error and can still submit complete arguments to the original tools. Continuation state is tied to the original tool and parameters, lasts ten minutes, and is consumed once. Concurrent or repeated answers cannot repeat the same operation. Restart invalidates pending input rather than replaying it.","locale":"en"},"2304":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction-11","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction#client-compatibility","content":"Input completion collects missing data; **it is not a general approval gate for writes**. Authorization for existing calls remains the client's policy.","locale":"en"},"2305":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction-12","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction#preview-a-message-draft","content":"Call `preview_message` with:","locale":"en"},"2306":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction-13","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction#preview-a-message-draft","content":"Use `private` for a private conversation. Targets must be positive safe integers. Optional reply IDs are non-zero signed 32-bit integers; negative values are valid. Only literal text and quoted replies are supported. Text resembling control codes is not interpreted as message segments.","locale":"en"},"2307":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction-14","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction#preview-a-message-draft","content":"Every client receives a readable draft, `can_send`, and the corresponding `invoke_action` arguments. Previewing sends nothing and does not fetch the quoted message.","locale":"en"},"2308":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction-15","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction#interactive-panel","content":"Clients declaring the MCP Apps extension `io.modelcontextprotocol/ui` and the `text/html;profile=mcp-app` MIME type receive the `ui://snowluma/message-preview.html` resource metadata.","locale":"en"},"2309":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction-16","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction#interactive-panel","content":"The panel shows the target, text, and quoted ID. It invokes the existing `invoke_action` through the host only after a user clicks Send; the server still enforces write permission. Read/docs mode and clients without server-tool support remain preview-only.","locale":"en"},"2310":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction-17","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/interaction#interactive-panel","content":"The panel prevents duplicate clicks and never retries failed or uncertain sends automatically. A successful acknowledgement means the server accepted the message, not proof of delivery or QQ rendering. The panel loads no external scripts, fonts, or media. Clients without panel support continue using text results.","locale":"en"},"2311":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","type":"page","content":"File Transfers and Background Tasks","breadcrumbs":["Docs","MCP"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","locale":"en"},"2312":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-0","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","content":"Transfer files between MCP and SnowLuma hosts and retain background task results","locale":"en"},"2313":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-1","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#choose-an-execution-method","content":"Choose an execution method","locale":"en"},"2314":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-2","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#upload-from-the-mcp-host","content":"Upload from the MCP host","locale":"en"},"2315":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-3","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#download-to-the-mcp-host","content":"Download to the MCP host","locale":"en"},"2316":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-4","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#progress-and-cancellation","content":"Progress and cancellation","locale":"en"},"2317":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-5","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#enable-persistent-tasks","content":"Enable persistent tasks","locale":"en"},"2318":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-6","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#restart-and-storage-boundaries","content":"Restart and storage boundaries","locale":"en"},"2319":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-7","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#choose-an-execution-method","content":"Ordinary `invoke_action` waits for completion. `invoke_action_background` persists a task record, returns its identifier, and lets the client fetch the result later. The background entry currently accepts only catalog actions marked as streams, not ordinary actions such as sending a message.","locale":"en"},"2320":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-8","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#choose-an-execution-method","content":"Both require write mode. Existing execution tools retain their behavior; background execution is an explicit choice.","locale":"en"},"2321":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-9","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#upload-from-the-mcp-host","content":"Set `SNOWLUMA_MCP_UPLOAD_ROOT` to an existing allowed directory. Pass these arguments to `invoke_action`:","locale":"en"},"2322":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-10","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#upload-from-the-mcp-host","content":"The input must resolve inside the upload root; paths and symlinks escaping it are rejected. MCP owns transfer identifiers and chunk fields; do not supply them again in `params`. `execution` controls MCP-side behavior and is not forwarded as action parameters.","locale":"en"},"2323":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-11","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#upload-from-the-mcp-host","content":"The completed `file_path` belongs to the **SnowLuma server** and can be used in a later media or file action. Uploading alone does not send a chat message. `file_retention` is in milliseconds and defaults to five minutes; zero disables expiry of the completed server file.","locale":"en"},"2324":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-12","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#upload-from-the-mcp-host","content":"Failure or cancellation attempts to clean up an unfinished upload, but cannot undo a committed file. A lost completion response may leave the remote file present. Do not blindly retry a send because the response was lost.","locale":"en"},"2325":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-13","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#download-to-the-mcp-host","content":"Example `invoke_action` arguments, with a **server-side** path:","locale":"en"},"2326":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-14","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#download-to-the-mcp-host","content":"A `file_id` may also be used as documented by the action. Image and record variants are `download_file_image_stream` and `download_file_record_stream`. Downloads are written incrementally under `SNOWLUMA_MCP_STREAM_DIR` and committed only after validation. Results contain `file_path`, `file_size`, `sha256`, `frame_count`, and `terminal`. This path is on the **MCP host**; the model does not receive the whole encoded file.","locale":"en"},"2327":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-15","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#download-to-the-mcp-host","content":"Each client allows four concurrent top-level streams. `SNOWLUMA_MCP_MAX_STREAM_BYTES` limits each file; the shared download directory quota is twice that value. Unknown-size downloads reserve the full per-file limit. Completed files remain on disk and consume quota until the operator moves or deletes them. Malformed frames, truncation, limit violations, and cancellation remove the unfinished download.","locale":"en"},"2328":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-16","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#progress-and-cancellation","content":"Supply standard `_meta.progressToken` metadata to receive matching `notifications/progress`. Downloads report bytes written, automatic uploads report acknowledged bytes, and generic streams report frame counts. Totals are present only for known positive file sizes. Calls without a progress token receive no progress notifications.","locale":"en"},"2329":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-17","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#progress-and-cancellation","content":"Cancellation reaches requests and response reads. Ordinary calls use a request timeout; streams use connection and per-read idle deadlines. Cancellation does not prove a remote operation was prevented, and progress does not replace a successful final result. Background tasks use status polling rather than the initiating request's progress or cancellation signal; cancel them with `tasks/cancel`.","locale":"en"},"2330":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-18","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#enable-persistent-tasks","content":"Requirements:","locale":"en"},"2331":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-19","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#enable-persistent-tasks","content":"Write mode with a OneBot HTTP endpoint.","locale":"en"},"2332":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-20","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#enable-persistent-tasks","content":"An absolute private `SNOWLUMA_MCP_TASK_DIR`. POSIX directories use `0700` and files `0600`; unsuitable permissions cause errors.","locale":"en"},"2333":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-21","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#enable-persistent-tasks","content":"An MCP `2026-07-28` client declaring `extensions: {\"io.modelcontextprotocol/tasks\": {}}`.","locale":"en"},"2334":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-22","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#enable-persistent-tasks","content":"Pass the same upload arguments to `invoke_action_background`. Its response resembles:","locale":"en"},"2335":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-23","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#enable-persistent-tasks","content":"The identifier above is illustrative; use the real returned value.","locale":"en"},"2336":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-24","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#enable-persistent-tasks","content":"Interface","locale":"en"},"2337":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-25","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#enable-persistent-tasks","content":"Purpose","locale":"en"},"2338":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-26","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#enable-persistent-tasks","content":"`tasks/get`, `{ \"taskId\": \"...\" }`","locale":"en"},"2339":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-27","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#enable-persistent-tasks","content":"Fetch status and the final saved `result` or `error`.","locale":"en"},"2340":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-28","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#enable-persistent-tasks","content":"`tasks/cancel`, `{ \"taskId\": \"...\" }`","locale":"en"},"2341":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-29","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#enable-persistent-tasks","content":"Request cooperative cancellation, then query the final state.","locale":"en"},"2342":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-30","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#enable-persistent-tasks","content":"`tasks/update`","locale":"en"},"2343":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-31","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#enable-persistent-tasks","content":"Answer outstanding task input requests, not edit arbitrary task fields.","locale":"en"},"2344":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-32","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#enable-persistent-tasks","content":"`list_tasks` tool","locale":"en"},"2345":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-33","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#enable-persistent-tasks","content":"List metadata without result bodies using `cursor` and `limit` (1–100, default 50).","locale":"en"},"2346":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-34","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#enable-persistent-tasks","content":"The current transfer entry does not request interactive input or automatically combine with `_with_input`; provide complete parameters first. Task lifecycle operations are protocol methods, while `list_tasks` is a tool. Deprecated `tasks/list` and `tasks/result` are not provided.","locale":"en"},"2347":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-35","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#enable-persistent-tasks","content":"`completed` means the tool finished, not necessarily that the business operation succeeded. Inspect nested diagnostics and OneBot responses. Cancellation does not roll back effects, and completion already in flight may win the race.","locale":"en"},"2348":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-36","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#restart-and-storage-boundaries","content":"Records survive restart without automatic expiry or deletion. &#x2A;*Unfinished work becomes failed with an unknown remote outcome; it is never replayed and transfers are not resumed.** At most four tasks run concurrently, with a 16 MiB limit per persisted record.","locale":"en"},"2349":{"id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers-37","page_id":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/mcp/transfers#restart-and-storage-boundaries","content":"A directory has one runtime owner and is bound to a digest of the effective mode, endpoint, and token. Use a new private directory when configuration changes, retaining old history. Do not delete records to hide configuration errors. Corruption, permission problems, and write failures remain explicit errors. Results may contain private account data.","locale":"en"},"2350":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","type":"page","content":"SDK","breadcrumbs":["Docs","SDK"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/sdk","locale":"en"},"2351":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-0","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk","content":"@snowluma/sdk — a typed OneBot client, independent of the SnowLuma runtime","locale":"en"},"2352":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-1","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/sdk#install","content":"Install","locale":"en"},"2353":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-2","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/sdk#supported-transports","content":"Supported transports","locale":"en"},"2354":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-3","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/sdk#constructing-a-client","content":"Constructing a client","locale":"en"},"2355":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-4","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/sdk#http","content":"HTTP","locale":"en"},"2356":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-5","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/sdk#websocket","content":"WebSocket","locale":"en"},"2357":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-6","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/sdk#calling-an-action","content":"Calling an action","locale":"en"},"2358":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-7","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/sdk#subscribing-to-events","content":"Subscribing to events","locale":"en"},"2359":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-8","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/sdk#account-online--offline","content":"Account online / offline","locale":"en"},"2360":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-9","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/sdk#message-builder","content":"Message builder","locale":"en"},"2361":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-10","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/sdk#auto-reconnect-ack-correlation-and-shared-types","content":"Auto-reconnect, ack correlation, and shared types","locale":"en"},"2362":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-11","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/sdk#subpath-imports","content":"Subpath imports","locale":"en"},"2363":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-12","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/sdk#see-also","content":"See also","locale":"en"},"2364":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-13","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk","content":"`@snowluma/sdk` is a **fully typed OneBot v11 client** written in TypeScript. It is built for downstream consumers: you don't run SnowLuma in the same process and you don't depend on the SnowLuma runtime — the SDK just connects to any running SnowLuma instance over its OneBot HTTP / WebSocket ports.","locale":"en"},"2365":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-14","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk","content":"The package installs from npm. The SDK maintains action names, parameter types, and result types independently, with tests against the server's action registry and parameter parsers. The published package does not import server code. The connected server version must still support the capabilities you use.","locale":"en"},"2366":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-15","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk","content":"This chapter follows the current SDK source. Availability in your installation depends on the npm package version you installed; source changes may not be published yet. Check both your SDK and SnowLuma server versions.","locale":"en"},"2367":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-16","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk","content":"Goal","locale":"en"},"2368":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-17","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk","content":"Start here","locale":"en"},"2369":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-18","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk","content":"Install, connect, call actions, subscribe to events","locale":"en"},"2370":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-19","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk","content":"This page","locale":"en"},"2371":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-20","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk","content":"Send local media, quote a message, wait for the next message","locale":"en"},"2372":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-21","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk","content":"Messaging helpers","locale":"en"},"2373":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-22","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk","content":"Upload and download incrementally, handle cancellation and transfer errors","locale":"en"},"2374":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-23","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk","content":"Streaming files","locale":"en"},"2375":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-24","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk","content":"The SDK connects to the OneBot ports SnowLuma exposes: commonly HTTP at `http://127.0.0.1:3000/` and WebSocket at `ws://127.0.0.1:3001/`. Use the addresses from your server configuration. The `accessToken` also comes from the OneBot config. Make sure those network adapters are enabled first on the Configuration page.","locale":"en"},"2376":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-25","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#install","content":"Requires &#x2A;*Node.js `^24.22.1 || >=26.12.1`**: Node 24 starting at 24.22.1, or 26.12.1 and later; Node 25 is excluded. The package is pure ESM (`\"type\": \"module\"`), ships type declarations, and supports native Node.js imports without a bundler.","locale":"en"},"2377":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-26","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#install","content":"Save this as `example.mjs` and run `node example.mjs` after installation:","locale":"en"},"2378":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-27","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#install","content":"TypeScript projects can use `module` / `moduleResolution: \"NodeNext\"` and set `\"type\": \"module\"` in their own `package.json`. Bundler-based projects are also supported.","locale":"en"},"2379":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-28","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#supported-transports","content":"Transport","locale":"en"},"2380":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-29","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#supported-transports","content":"Client class","locale":"en"},"2381":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-30","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#supported-transports","content":"Default endpoint","locale":"en"},"2382":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-31","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#supported-transports","content":"HTTP (POST JSON)","locale":"en"},"2383":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-32","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#supported-transports","content":"`SnowLumaHttpClient`","locale":"en"},"2384":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-33","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#supported-transports","content":"`http://127.0.0.1:3000/`","locale":"en"},"2385":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-34","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#supported-transports","content":"WebSocket (outbound connection, with events)","locale":"en"},"2386":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-35","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#supported-transports","content":"`SnowLumaWebSocketClient`","locale":"en"},"2387":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-36","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#supported-transports","content":"`ws://127.0.0.1:3001/`","locale":"en"},"2388":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-37","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#supported-transports","content":"Both clients extend the abstract `SnowLumaApiClient` base, so `call()` / `request()` and every camelCase action shortcut work identically across transports. HTTP suits plain request/response scripts; WebSocket adds **realtime event delivery** on top. `SnowLumaWebSocketClient` connects to a forward WebSocket endpoint; it does not provide a listening server for reverse WebSocket connections.","locale":"en"},"2389":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-38","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#http","content":"`SnowLumaHttpClientOptions`:","locale":"en"},"2390":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-39","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#http","content":"`baseUrl?` — OneBot HTTP endpoint, defaults to `http://127.0.0.1:3000/`.","locale":"en"},"2391":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-40","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#http","content":"`accessToken?` — token from the OneBot config; when set, an `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header is sent automatically.","locale":"en"},"2392":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-41","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#http","content":"`requestTimeoutMs?` — default timeout in ms, defaults to `30000`.","locale":"en"},"2393":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-42","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#http","content":"`fetch?` — custom `fetch` implementation (tests or non-standard runtimes).","locale":"en"},"2394":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-43","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#http","content":"`headers?` — extra headers attached to every request.","locale":"en"},"2395":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-44","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#websocket","content":"`SnowLumaWebSocketClientOptions`:","locale":"en"},"2396":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-45","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#websocket","content":"`url?` — OneBot WebSocket endpoint, defaults to `ws://127.0.0.1:3001/`.","locale":"en"},"2397":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-46","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#websocket","content":"`accessToken?` — appended to the connection URL as a query parameter.","locale":"en"},"2398":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-47","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#websocket","content":"`requestTimeoutMs?` — default request timeout, defaults to `30000`.","locale":"en"},"2399":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-48","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#websocket","content":"`role?` — a retained client property: `'Api'` | `'Event'` | `'Universal'` (default `'Universal'`). It is currently not sent to the server and does not select endpoint permissions or event routing.","locale":"en"},"2400":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-49","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#websocket","content":"`reconnect?` — `true` or a `ReconnectOptions` (`retries` / `minDelayMs` / `maxDelayMs`) to enable auto-reconnect after an unexpected close.","locale":"en"},"2401":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-50","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#websocket","content":"`protocols?` / `webSocket?` — optional subprotocols, optional custom `WebSocket` constructor (Node runtimes or tests).","locale":"en"},"2402":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-51","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#websocket","content":"Browsers and Node 24 ship a global `WebSocket` that works out of the box. To use an implementation like the `ws` package, pass it to the `webSocket` option.","locale":"en"},"2403":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-52","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#websocket","content":"> The factory functions `createHttpClient(options?)` and `createWebSocketClient(options?)` are equivalent to `new`; use whichever you prefer.","locale":"en"},"2404":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-53","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#calling-an-action","content":"Common endpoints have fully typed camelCase methods (`getLoginInfo`, `sendGroupMessage`, `setGroupBan`, …). Any registered action can be called via `raw` / `rawResponse`.","locale":"en"},"2405":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-54","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#calling-an-action","content":"The underlying methods:","locale":"en"},"2406":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-55","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#calling-an-action","content":"`call(action, params?, options?)` — sends the action and returns `data`; throws `SnowLumaApiError` when `status` is `failed` or `retcode !== 0`.","locale":"en"},"2407":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-56","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#calling-an-action","content":"`request(action, params?, options?)` — returns the full response envelope and does not throw on business errors.","locale":"en"},"2408":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-57","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#calling-an-action","content":"Every known action has a parameter and result entry in `SnowLumaActionMap`, including compatibility aliases. Use `ActionParams<ActionName>` and `ActionResult<ActionName>` in your own wrappers. Some results retain broad JSON contracts for compatibility; static types do not replace server-side range, permission, or state validation.","locale":"en"},"2409":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-58","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#calling-an-action","content":"Every request can override behavior via `RequestOptions`: `echo` (correlation value), `timeoutMs` (`0` disables the timeout), and `signal` (an `AbortSignal`).","locale":"en"},"2410":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-59","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#subscribing-to-events","content":"Event subscription is a WebSocket-client capability. The client correlates API responses by `echo` and dispatches packets without an `echo` as events.","locale":"en"},"2411":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-60","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#subscribing-to-events","content":"Available event helpers: `onMessage` / `onPrivateMessage` / `onGroupMessage` / `onNotice(type?)` / `onBotStatus` / `onRequest(type?)` / `onMetaEvent` / `command()`, plus the lower-level `onEvent`, `when(predicate, handler)`, and `use(middleware)`. Lifecycle events use `on('open' | 'close' | 'error' | 'response' | 'raw', …)`. Every `on` / `when` / `use` returns an unsubscribe function.","locale":"en"},"2412":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-61","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#account-online--offline","content":"When an account comes online or goes offline, SnowLuma pushes a notice. `sub_type` is `online` or `offline`. A forced kick is still `bot_offline`. Process exit does not emit `offline`.","locale":"en"},"2413":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-62","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#account-online--offline","content":"This is separate from the email / webhook channels under WebUI Settings → Notifications. Those are for operators without a bot. If you have a bot, listen here and send the alert wherever you want.","locale":"en"},"2414":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-63","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#account-online--offline","content":"You can also use `bot.onNotice('bot_status', handler)` or `isBotStatusEvent`.","locale":"en"},"2415":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-64","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#account-online--offline","content":"The event context (`ctx`) has built-in shortcuts:","locale":"en"},"2416":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-65","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#account-online--offline","content":"`ctx.reply(message)` — sends an ordinary reply to the private/group conversation.","locale":"en"},"2417":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-66","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#account-online--offline","content":"`ctx.quote(message)` — quotes the current message from an SDK-created message-event context; see Messaging helpers.","locale":"en"},"2418":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-67","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#account-online--offline","content":"`ctx.approve()` / `ctx.reject(reason)` — handle friend or group requests.","locale":"en"},"2419":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-68","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#account-online--offline","content":"`ctx.quickOperation(operation)` — calls `.handle_quick_operation`.","locale":"en"},"2420":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-69","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#account-online--offline","content":"`ctx.stopPropagation()` — stops further middleware dispatch.","locale":"en"},"2421":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-70","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#message-builder","content":"The SDK ships a chainable message builder and segment factories; send methods accept their output directly:","locale":"en"},"2422":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-71","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#message-builder","content":"Built-in segments: `text`, `br`, `face`, `at`, `atAll`, `reply`, `image`, `record`, `video`, `json`, `xml`, `poke`, `forward`, `node`, `share`, `music`, `location`, `contact`, `raw`. `reply()` may appear only once per chain.","locale":"en"},"2423":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-72","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#message-builder","content":"String file paths inside message segments, such as `/tmp/a.png` above, refer to the **SnowLuma server**. They do not read files from the SDK machine; use the local media helpers for that. Message IDs are non-zero signed 32-bit integers, so negative values are valid. Preserve their sign when quoting, querying, or deleting messages.","locale":"en"},"2424":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-73","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#auto-reconnect-ack-correlation-and-shared-types","content":"**Ack correlation** — the WebSocket client generates an `echo` per request and routes the response back to the right `Promise`, so concurrent requests never cross. Override the correlation value via `RequestOptions.echo`.","locale":"en"},"2425":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-74","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#auto-reconnect-ack-correlation-and-shared-types","content":"**Auto-reconnect** — `reconnect: true` (or a `ReconnectOptions`) enables exponential backoff (`minDelayMs` defaults to 1000, `maxDelayMs` to 30000). On disconnect, all pending requests reject with `SnowLumaConnectionError`.","locale":"en"},"2426":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-75","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#auto-reconnect-ack-correlation-and-shared-types","content":"**Type compatibility** — consumers can share the SDK's exported types, but they are maintained independently of server code. The bundled catalog lists actions known to that SDK version; it does not probe the remote server's capabilities. Custom or dynamic actions remain available through `raw()` / `rawResponse()`.","locale":"en"},"2427":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-76","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#auto-reconnect-ack-correlation-and-shared-types","content":"**Business and transport errors** — SDK business and transport error classes extend `SnowLumaError`: business failures throw `SnowLumaApiError` (auth-class retcodes become `SnowLumaAuthError`); transport issues throw the `SnowLumaTransportError` subclasses `SnowLumaConnectionError` / `SnowLumaParseError` / `SnowLumaTimeoutError` / `SnowLumaAbortError`. Local validation, file access, and some context operations can also throw native exceptions, so handling only `SnowLumaError` is insufficient.","locale":"en"},"2428":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-77","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#subpath-imports","content":"Beyond the main entry, the package exposes per-module exports: `@snowluma/sdk/client`, `/messages`, `/events`, `/types`, `/errors`, `/actions`, and `/node`. Import only what you need.","locale":"en"},"2429":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-78","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#subpath-imports","content":"`SNOWLUMA_ACTIONS`, `isSnowLumaAction`, and the `SnowLumaKnownAction` type are available from either the root entry or `/actions`. The optional `/node` entry provides `localFile()` for local files; root and browser-facing entries do not import Node filesystem modules.","locale":"en"},"2430":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-79","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#see-also","content":"Messaging helpers — local media sends, quoted replies, and event waits.","locale":"en"},"2431":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-80","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#see-also","content":"Streaming files — uploads, downloads, progress, and cancellation.","locale":"en"},"2432":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-81","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#see-also","content":"Configuration — enable and secure the OneBot HTTP / WS adapters and get an `accessToken`.","locale":"en"},"2433":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-82","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#see-also","content":"Developer guide — monorepo layout and runtime internals.","locale":"en"},"2434":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk-83","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk#see-also","content":"MCP server — an alternative integration path for LLMs.","locale":"en"},"2435":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","type":"page","content":"Messaging helpers","breadcrumbs":["Docs","SDK"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","locale":"en"},"2436":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-0","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","content":"Send local media, quote messages explicitly, and wait for future events","locale":"en"},"2437":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-1","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#send-local-media-in-one-call","content":"Send local media in one call","locale":"en"},"2438":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-2","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#send-a-file-from-nodejs","content":"Send a file from Node.js","locale":"en"},"2439":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-3","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#bytes-browser-files-and-streams","content":"Bytes, browser files, and streams","locale":"en"},"2440":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-4","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#errors-and-cancellation","content":"Errors and cancellation","locale":"en"},"2441":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-5","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#quote-a-message-explicitly","content":"Quote a message explicitly","locale":"en"},"2442":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-6","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#wait-for-a-future-event","content":"Wait for a future event","locale":"en"},"2443":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-7","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","content":"These helpers preserve existing behavior: string paths in message segments still refer to the SnowLuma server, `ctx.reply()` still sends an ordinary reply, and existing subscriptions and middleware need no migration.","locale":"en"},"2444":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-8","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","content":"This page follows the current SDK source; availability depends on your installed npm release. Configure a client using the SDK overview first. Media sends also require a SnowLuma server that supports streaming uploads and the corresponding send actions.","locale":"en"},"2445":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-9","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#send-local-media-in-one-call","content":"Both HTTP and WebSocket clients provide these methods. They upload local bytes, wait for completion, then pass the returned server path to the send action.","locale":"en"},"2446":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-10","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#send-local-media-in-one-call","content":"Content","locale":"en"},"2447":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-11","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#send-local-media-in-one-call","content":"Group method","locale":"en"},"2448":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-12","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#send-local-media-in-one-call","content":"Private method","locale":"en"},"2449":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-13","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#send-local-media-in-one-call","content":"Result","locale":"en"},"2450":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-14","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#send-local-media-in-one-call","content":"Image","locale":"en"},"2451":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-15","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#send-local-media-in-one-call","content":"`sendGroupImage`","locale":"en"},"2452":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-16","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#send-local-media-in-one-call","content":"`sendPrivateImage`","locale":"en"},"2453":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-17","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#send-local-media-in-one-call","content":"`{ message_id }`","locale":"en"},"2454":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-18","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#send-local-media-in-one-call","content":"Voice","locale":"en"},"2455":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-19","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#send-local-media-in-one-call","content":"`sendGroupRecord`","locale":"en"},"2456":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-20","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#send-local-media-in-one-call","content":"`sendPrivateRecord`","locale":"en"},"2457":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-21","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#send-local-media-in-one-call","content":"`{ message_id }`","locale":"en"},"2458":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-22","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#send-local-media-in-one-call","content":"Video","locale":"en"},"2459":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-23","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#send-local-media-in-one-call","content":"`sendGroupVideo`","locale":"en"},"2460":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-24","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#send-local-media-in-one-call","content":"`sendPrivateVideo`","locale":"en"},"2461":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-25","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#send-local-media-in-one-call","content":"`{ message_id }`","locale":"en"},"2462":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-26","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#send-local-media-in-one-call","content":"File","locale":"en"},"2463":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-27","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#send-local-media-in-one-call","content":"`sendGroupFile`","locale":"en"},"2464":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-28","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#send-local-media-in-one-call","content":"`sendPrivateFile`","locale":"en"},"2465":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-29","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#send-local-media-in-one-call","content":"`{ file_id }`","locale":"en"},"2466":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-30","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#send-a-file-from-nodejs","content":"`localFile(pathOrFileURL)` is available &#x2A;*only from `@snowluma/sdk/node`**. It returns a named, file-backed `Blob` source without buffering the entire file. The path is on the SDK machine. Keep the file unchanged until sending finishes: missing files, non-regular files, and changes during reading produce errors. Root and browser-facing entries do not import Node filesystem modules.","locale":"en"},"2467":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-31","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#bytes-browser-files-and-streams","content":"Media sources support:","locale":"en"},"2468":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-32","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#bytes-browser-files-and-streams","content":"`Uint8Array`, including Node.js `Buffer`.","locale":"en"},"2469":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-33","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#bytes-browser-files-and-streams","content":"`Blob` or a browser-selected `File`; a `File` supplies its name automatically.","locale":"en"},"2470":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-34","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#bytes-browser-files-and-streams","content":"`ReadableStream<Uint8Array>` or `AsyncIterable<Uint8Array>`, including byte-mode Node.js readable streams; these require `fileSize`.","locale":"en"},"2471":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-35","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#bytes-browser-files-and-streams","content":"`{ source, filename }`, to name a source without changing its bytes.","locale":"en"},"2472":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-36","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#bytes-browser-files-and-streams","content":"An explicit `filename` option overrides the source's name. For file sends, `name` is the display name in QQ and defaults to the uploaded filename; group files also accept `folder` / `folderId`.","locale":"en"},"2473":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-37","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#bytes-browser-files-and-streams","content":"Put media attributes under `image`, `record`, or `video`. `video.thumb` remains a **server-side path**; thumbnails are not uploaded automatically. These new methods do not accept a local-path string: use `localFile()` explicitly or provide a byte source.","locale":"en"},"2474":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-38","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#bytes-browser-files-and-streams","content":"See Streaming files for upload options, including `chunkSize`, `expectedSha256`, `fileRetention`, `signal`, and `onProgress`. Progress counts bytes acknowledged by the server, not QQ message delivery.","locale":"en"},"2475":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-39","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#errors-and-cancellation","content":"`SnowLumaMediaSendError.stage` is `upload` or `send`. Its `cause` retains the original API, abort, or timeout error, and `upload` contains metadata when the upload completed. Errors opening a file with `localFile()` are thrown directly rather than wrapped as send errors.","locale":"en"},"2476":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-40","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#errors-and-cancellation","content":"`timeoutMs` applies separately to each upload request and the final send request; it is not a deadline for the whole operation or source reads. Use your own `AbortSignal` for overall cancellation. Cancellation between the stages prevents sending. Cancellation or timeout after dispatch does not prove that a message was not sent. The SDK does not retry automatically, roll back, or delete server files. Failed group-file chat publication is reported as an error with the uploaded file ID retained in its error context.","locale":"en"},"2477":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-41","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#quote-a-message-explicitly","content":"Use `ctx.quote()` in an SDK-created message-event context to quote the current message. Ordinary `ctx.reply()` behavior remains unchanged.","locale":"en"},"2478":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-42","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#quote-a-message-explicitly","content":"`ctx.quote()` chooses the event's private or group conversation and uses its message ID. It rejects non-message events. Outside a handler, including with an HTTP client, use `quoteMessage()` to compose the same content:","locale":"en"},"2479":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-43","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#quote-a-message-explicitly","content":"`quoteMessage(messageId, body, options?)` is also exported from `@snowluma/sdk/messages`. It only composes content; it does not query history or send requests. The server must be able to resolve the referenced message ID. IDs must be **non-zero signed 32-bit integers**; negative values are preserved.","locale":"en"},"2480":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-44","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#quote-a-message-explicitly","content":"Bodies accept plain strings, CQ strings, a single segment, segment arrays, or message chains. String CQ fields and escaping are preserved by default. With `autoEscape: true`, a string becomes literal text following the quote; arrays and chains remain structured. A body already containing a reply segment is rejected. Inputs are not mutated.","locale":"en"},"2481":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-45","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#quote-a-message-explicitly","content":"Old `SnowLumaEventContext` objects and explicitly typed existing handlers remain valid. SDK-created contexts and inferred client callbacks expose `SnowLumaEventContextWithQuote`. To annotate a reusable new handler, use `EventHandler<MyEvent, SnowLumaEventContextWithQuote<MyEvent>>`; middleware and command handlers provide the corresponding context type parameter as well.","locale":"en"},"2482":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-46","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#wait-for-a-future-event","content":"The WebSocket client provides `waitForEvent(predicate?, options?)` and `waitForMessage(predicate?, options?)`, and both also accept just an options object. Predicates must return a boolean synchronously. Type guards additionally narrow the resolved type.","locale":"en"},"2483":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-47","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#wait-for-a-future-event","content":"Register the wait before sending so a fast reply cannot arrive before its listener:","locale":"en"},"2484":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-48","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#wait-for-a-future-event","content":"Waits register synchronously. They do not connect automatically, replay history, consume other listeners' events, or survive reconnects. They observe the same public stream as `onEvent`, **after middleware**; events stopped by middleware are not visible. Multiple waits can resolve from the same event.","locale":"en"},"2485":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-49","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#wait-for-a-future-event","content":"`waitForMessage` includes both `message` and `message_sent`. To wait only for an incoming reply, filter direction, conversation, and sender as in the example.","locale":"en"},"2486":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-50","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#wait-for-a-future-event","content":"Outcome","locale":"en"},"2487":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-51","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#wait-for-a-future-event","content":"Behavior","locale":"en"},"2488":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-52","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#wait-for-a-future-event","content":"Predicate matches","locale":"en"},"2489":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-53","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#wait-for-a-future-event","content":"Resolves with the event and removes the listener, abort handler, and timer","locale":"en"},"2490":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-54","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#wait-for-a-future-event","content":"Timeout","locale":"en"},"2491":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-55","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#wait-for-a-future-event","content":"Rejects with `SnowLumaTimeoutError`","locale":"en"},"2492":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-56","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#wait-for-a-future-event","content":"`signal` cancellation","locale":"en"},"2493":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-57","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#wait-for-a-future-event","content":"Rejects with `SnowLumaAbortError`","locale":"en"},"2494":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-58","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#wait-for-a-future-event","content":"Disconnection or explicit `close()`","locale":"en"},"2495":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-59","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#wait-for-a-future-event","content":"Rejects with `SnowLumaConnectionError`; reconnect does not restore the wait","locale":"en"},"2496":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-60","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#wait-for-a-future-event","content":"Predicate throws","locale":"en"},"2497":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-61","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#wait-for-a-future-event","content":"Rejects with the original error","locale":"en"},"2498":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging-62","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/messaging#wait-for-a-future-event","content":"Every completion path cleans up listeners and timers. The default timeout is the client's `requestTimeoutMs` (30 seconds by default); `0` disables it. Cancelling a wait does not itself close the client or undo a sent message. The example explicitly closes its connection in `finally`.","locale":"en"},"2499":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","type":"page","content":"Streaming files","breadcrumbs":["Docs","SDK"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","locale":"en"},"2500":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-0","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","content":"Incremental uploads, chunked downloads, cancellation, validation, and errors","locale":"en"},"2501":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-1","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#upload-a-file","content":"Upload a file","locale":"en"},"2502":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-2","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#download-a-file","content":"Download a file","locale":"en"},"2503":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-3","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#read-individual-frames","content":"Read individual frames","locale":"en"},"2504":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-4","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#cancellation-timeouts-and-buffering","content":"Cancellation, timeouts, and buffering","locale":"en"},"2505":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-5","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","content":"Both HTTP and WebSocket clients support streaming uploads and downloads. Existing `request()`, `call()`, `raw()`, `rawResponse()`, and `downloadFile()` keep their single-response contracts; use the methods below for responses containing multiple frames. To upload and immediately send media, see Messaging helpers.","locale":"en"},"2506":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-6","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","content":"This page follows the current SDK source; availability depends on your installed npm release. The connected SnowLuma server must also support the relevant streaming actions. See the SDK overview for installation and configuration.","locale":"en"},"2507":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-7","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#upload-a-file","content":"`uploadFileStream(source, options?)` uploads incrementally, waits for each chunk acknowledgement, then issues a separate completion request. It returns `UploadFileStreamComplete`, including `file_path`, `file_size`, and `sha256`.","locale":"en"},"2508":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-8","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#upload-a-file","content":"`source` accepts `Uint8Array` (including Node.js `Buffer`), `Blob`, `ReadableStream<Uint8Array>`, or `AsyncIterable<Uint8Array>`. Byte arrays and blobs provide their size. Streams and async iterables require `fileSize` so the total chunk count is known before uploading. A mismatch between actual and declared length throws. Empty files are supported.","locale":"en"},"2509":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-9","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#upload-a-file","content":"Option","locale":"en"},"2510":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-10","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#upload-a-file","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"2511":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-11","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#upload-a-file","content":"`fileSize`","locale":"en"},"2512":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-12","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#upload-a-file","content":"Total byte count; required for stream sources","locale":"en"},"2513":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-13","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#upload-a-file","content":"`filename`","locale":"en"},"2514":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-14","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#upload-a-file","content":"Uploaded filename","locale":"en"},"2515":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-15","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#upload-a-file","content":"`chunkSize`","locale":"en"},"2516":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-16","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#upload-a-file","content":"Decoded bytes per chunk; defaults to 64 KiB, range 1–1048576","locale":"en"},"2517":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-17","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#upload-a-file","content":"`expectedSha256`","locale":"en"},"2518":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-18","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#upload-a-file","content":"Expected digest, verified by the server and checked against completion metadata by the SDK","locale":"en"},"2519":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-19","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#upload-a-file","content":"`fileRetention`","locale":"en"},"2520":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-20","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#upload-a-file","content":"Completed server-file retention in milliseconds; `0` disables expiry; the current server default is five minutes","locale":"en"},"2521":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-21","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#upload-a-file","content":"`streamId`","locale":"en"},"2522":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-22","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#upload-a-file","content":"Unique ID for a fresh upload; generated when omitted; must not reuse an existing upload","locale":"en"},"2523":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-23","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#upload-a-file","content":"`onProgress`","locale":"en"},"2524":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-24","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#upload-a-file","content":"Called after each acknowledged chunk; may return a Promise, which is awaited before reading more","locale":"en"},"2525":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-25","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#upload-a-file","content":"`signal` / `timeoutMs` / `echo`","locale":"en"},"2526":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-26","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#upload-a-file","content":"Request cancellation, timeout, and correlation value; see the boundaries below","locale":"en"},"2527":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-27","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#upload-a-file","content":"`file_path` is on the **SnowLuma server**. Upload completion does not write a file on the SDK machine or send a QQ message. The helper does not resume or retry transfers automatically.","locale":"en"},"2528":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-28","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#upload-a-file","content":"`signal` cancels requests and closes readable sources. Custom async iterables should receive the same signal so pending reads and cleanup can finish. The SDK cannot force an arbitrary producer to resolve its promises. The example passes the same signal to the Node.js source.","locale":"en"},"2529":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-29","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#upload-a-file","content":"Failed or cancelled uploads are not finalized. Partial uploads expire after the server's idle timeout (currently ten minutes). The SDK does not issue a reset request or delete completed server files automatically. Retention and partial-upload cleanup are server policies; check your deployed version.","locale":"en"},"2530":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-30","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#download-a-file","content":"`downloadFileStream(params, options?)` returns an async iterator yielding `Uint8Array` chunks. This Node.js example downloads to a separate temporary file and moves it to the target only after successful completion:","locale":"en"},"2531":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-31","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#download-a-file","content":"Parameters accept a server-side `file` or `file_id`, plus optional `chunk_size`. `options.action` selects `download_file_stream` (default), `download_file_image_stream`, or `download_file_record_stream`. `onInfo` runs before the first byte chunk is yielded.","locale":"en"},"2532":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-32","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#download-a-file","content":"The iterator's final return value is `DownloadFileStreamComplete`. `for await` and `pipeline()` consume and validate the transfer, but discard that return value. To access its `total_bytes` / `total_chunks`, call `iterator.next()` manually and read `value` when `done` is `true`.","locale":"en"},"2533":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-33","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#download-a-file","content":"The SDK decodes and checks chunk order, chunk lengths, and final totals. A zero initial size may mean unknown size; final byte and chunk counts must still match. Missing metadata, malformed frames, truncation, and server failures throw. Bytes already consumed by your application are not rolled back.","locale":"en"},"2534":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-34","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#read-individual-frames","content":"Use `stream()` or `requestStream()` when you need raw frame information:","locale":"en"},"2535":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-35","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#read-individual-frames","content":"`requestStream()` yields full response envelopes, including a final failed envelope. Callers check business success themselves.","locale":"en"},"2536":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-36","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#read-individual-frames","content":"`stream()` yields typed payloads and throws `SnowLumaApiError` or its authentication subtype for failed envelopes, even after earlier data has arrived.","locale":"en"},"2537":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-37","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#read-individual-frames","content":"Both support the three download actions, `test_download_stream`, and `upload_file_stream`. Each upload request returns one acknowledgement, including `type: 'stream'` chunk acknowledgements. Low-level callers finalize in a separate request. Reset retains the server's existing failed-envelope behavior.","locale":"en"},"2538":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-38","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#cancellation-timeouts-and-buffering","content":"`signal`, `echo`, and `timeoutMs` work as on ordinary requests. Timeout covers one active streaming request, including WebSocket connection setup. Uploads apply it separately to each chunk and completion request. `0` disables timeout. Source reads and application callbacks are not timed by the request timeout; use your own cancellation signal for an overall deadline.","locale":"en"},"2539":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-39","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#cancellation-timeouts-and-buffering","content":"Stopping iteration releases client resources. HTTP also cancels its response body. WebSocket stops collecting that request without closing the shared connection. The protocol has no per-request download cancellation message, so the server may continue sending remaining frames. Use unique transfer echoes; do not reuse an aborted transfer's echo while late frames may arrive. Disconnects fail active transfers, and reconnects do not replay them.","locale":"en"},"2540":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-40","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#cancellation-timeouts-and-buffering","content":"Option","locale":"en"},"2541":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-41","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#cancellation-timeouts-and-buffering","content":"Default","locale":"en"},"2542":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-42","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#cancellation-timeouts-and-buffering","content":"Limit","locale":"en"},"2543":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-43","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#cancellation-timeouts-and-buffering","content":"`maxBufferBytes`","locale":"en"},"2544":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-44","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#cancellation-timeouts-and-buffering","content":"32 MiB","locale":"en"},"2545":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-45","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#cancellation-timeouts-and-buffering","content":"One HTTP frame or queued WebSocket payload bytes","locale":"en"},"2546":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-46","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#cancellation-timeouts-and-buffering","content":"`maxBufferedFrames`","locale":"en"},"2547":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-47","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#cancellation-timeouts-and-buffering","content":"256","locale":"en"},"2548":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-48","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#cancellation-timeouts-and-buffering","content":"Queued WebSocket frames","locale":"en"},"2549":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-49","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#cancellation-timeouts-and-buffering","content":"Overflow throws instead of silently dropping frames or buffering the entire file. HTTP reads follow consumption; WebSocket has no per-request backpressure. Prefer HTTP when downloading large files to a slow destination.","locale":"en"},"2550":{"id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming-50","page_id":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/sdk/streaming#cancellation-timeouts-and-buffering","content":"Streaming types are exported from `@snowluma/sdk` and `@snowluma/sdk/types`. Custom `SnowLumaApiClient` subclasses can implement `requestStream()` to support streaming. Existing request-only subclasses remain compatible and receive an explicit unsupported error if streaming is attempted.","locale":"en"},"2551":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/baota","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/baota","type":"page","content":"BT Panel Deploy","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Deployment"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/baota","locale":"en"},"2552":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/baota-0","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/baota","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/baota","content":"One-click deploy SnowLuma via Docker App Store on a Linux server with BT Panel (Baota)","locale":"en"},"2553":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/baota-1","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/baota","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/baota#import--install","content":"Import & Install","locale":"en"},"2554":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/baota-2","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/baota","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/baota#first-login","content":"First Login","locale":"en"},"2555":{"id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/baota-3","page_id":"/en/docs/guide/deploy/baota","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":